														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3940611">
									

<p>The interviews are kinda prosey for my taste. People are a little too good at wordplay and cracking wise, sort of reminds me of the silly interview log from 106-ARC.</p>
<p>Re: the narrative, SCP-4669 seems way OP and doesn't fit the established Misters Against Weed M.O.&#8212;the original Little Misters all feel neatly interrelated, like siblings, whereas I can't imagine SCP-4669 having anything to do with Mr. Meme or Mr. Deadly Sins. There's just <em>too</em> much tonal variance in this family and I don't like it.</p>
<p>I describe myself as liking GAW, but I think my biggest issue w/ them is the constant tone shift between light silly articles about left-leaning internet culture, and heavy-handed epics about death and intrigue that are borderline tale-worthy. I prefer a GOI where I can open an article knowing &quot;oh, this is a Wondertainment article&quot;, or something, and know for mostly-certain what kind of article I'm gonna read. I just don't like articles structured like this.</p>
<p>And I know there is no canon, every article is its own universe/timeline, yadda yadda, but it's kinda ballsy to a god-modding degree to forecast GAW's fall from grace, like, ten years from present day. That level of certainty's kind of offputting.</p>

							</div>

								
